import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 675 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
rows = [
"| 676 | 2026-10-26 | **Hear and Sing Further, the first Grades 2-3 room (Build AJ).** Built on row 675. Board call 14 (her 14:31 \"너 추천대로 가자\": aural first). New chapter `listen-23` on the Grades 2-3 floor after Melody & Phrasing (PATH_STAGES floor 4 ids melody, listen-23, more-scales; more-scales still waits off the map, so listen-23 is the floor's last room for now and PathNext sends the child on to Stories of music). It is chapter 30, so The piano's story, Composers and Styles move to 31-33. The Grade 2 and 3 practical aural tests (Manual of Syllabuses 2026, section 21, read from the PDF), one step each: two notes played together, hum the higher or the lower (Grade 2: a major 3rd or a perfect 5th, Grade 3: any two notes, within an octave from middle C: L2_G2, L2_G3 on white keys, L2_QUAL names every pair incl. F-B the augmented 4th); the keynote then the 2nd, 3rd, 4th or 5th of the major scale, sung and named (Grade 3; keynotes C, D, F, G are our choice); clap back a passage heard twice, then say two or three (Grades 2-3; Grade 3 names it); sing back a longer phrase with its rhythm (L2_PH, 8 beats, skips and steps). Every test is heard twice, as the Manual says for grades above Preliminary, and the Manual makes a test's examples harder with each grade, so the passages add the dotted crotchet and quaver and the phrases are longer and wider than the Grade 1 room's (how much harder is our choice). No writing: the 'write' in the board's working name came from Music Craft's melodic dictation, which her 10:23 call made reference only; the practical aural tests have none. Pads L2DyadPad, L2DegPad, L2ClapPad, L2SingPad; drill levels dyad, any, deg, metre, clap, sing; Home: aural group au-23 (lessons l2-dyad, l2-any, l2-deg, l2-clap, l2-sing via l2Add/lwTapQ; l2DegQ a choice question with a keyboard after the answer), HOME_FLOOR '23'; Lesson Book of 7 pages (l2LbPages), teacher's copy L2Teacher (material to play for each page, C' = the C above), no Workbook (every step is by ear). Her metaphors only: higher is the bird's, lower the turtle's; walk, run-ning, hold. The app scores taps and answers; whether a child sang in tune stays the teacher's ear. Tests aj703.js, aj703b.js, chsweep, booksweep, reg674. |",
]
for r in reversed(rows): lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, r)
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
